# Code owners. GitHub reads the copy on the PR's base branch, so a PR can't weaken this file.
# The LAST matching pattern wins, so the sensitive paths stay at the bottom: if the default
# line is ever narrowed to layer or team owners, these still go to the owner.
#
# Required code-owner review is OFF in .github/rulesets/main.json until agents open PRs
# under a GitHub App: a PR author can't approve their own PR.

# Default owner
*                         @nehmetohme

# Sensitive paths: always the owner
/.github/                 @nehmetohme
/.claude/                 @nehmetohme
/contracts/               @nehmetohme
**/tests/contract_*       @nehmetohme
**/*.contract.test.ts     @nehmetohme
**/e2e/contract/          @nehmetohme
/backend/layers.toml      @nehmetohme
/backend/deny.toml        @nehmetohme
/justfile                 @nehmetohme
/lefthook.yml             @nehmetohme
/tools/                   @nehmetohme
